   "source": [
    "## SF-FSA-VI: composing the corner basis for a non-Markovian task, exactly\n",
    "\n",
    "This domain (Office) and this exact planning idea are from your own paper -- Kuric,\n",
    "Infante et al., *\"Planning with a Learned Policy Basis to Optimally Solve Complex\n",
    "Tasks\"* (ICAPS 2024), whose code lives in `RM/sf-fsa-vi`. Its `SFFSAValueIteration`\n",
    "(`fsa/planning.py`) solves a **non-Markovian** task -- specified as a finite state\n",
    "automaton (FSA) over propositions, e.g. \"coffee, then mail, then office\" (order\n",
    "matters, so no Markovian reward on the raw grid state can express it) -- *without*\n",
    "solving the full product MDP (grid state x automaton state). Instead it does backward\n",
    "value iteration over the tiny automaton graph itself: for each automaton state `u`, a\n",
    "weight vector `W[u]` where `W[u][idx] = 1` if satisfying proposition `idx` finishes the\n",
    "task, else the value of *continuing* from that proposition's exit state under the\n",
    "*next* automaton state's own weight vector -- queried from an already-trained GPI\n",
    "policy basis via `gpi.max_q(exit_state, w)`.\n",
    "\n",
    "`gpi.max_q(e, w)` is exactly `max_i max_a Pi_base[i][e] @ w` -- the same joint-argmax\n",
    "quantity `gpi_action` uses, just returning the winning SF vector instead of the action.\n",
    "So the direct port into this notebook's exact framework is `meta_fsa_value_iteration`\n",
    "below, calling `meta_policy_iteration_from_any` (an exact composition value, no neural\n",
    "net or approximation) wherever the paper calls `gpi.max_q`.\n",
    "\n",
    "**One real wrinkle, not just a renaming exercise.** `meta_policy_iteration` (Section\n",
    "\"Exact policy iteration over the composition\" above) treats every object cell as\n",
    "*absorbing* when building its linear system -- correct for the single-shot task it was\n",
    "built to solve exactly (nothing more to gain once you've already touched an object and\n",
    "that episode ended). But here we need the opposite: the value of *freshly starting* a\n",
    "new single-task episode *at* an exit state, continuing on to whatever's next. That's\n",
    "`meta_policy_iteration_from_any` -- identical machinery, just no longer skipping object\n",
    "cells as *source* states (they're still terminal as *destinations*, i.e. touching one\n",
    "still fires a reward and can still end a step). `Pi_corners` already has meaningful\n",
    "values there because `ADD_OBJ_TO_START=True` let training start episodes from those\n",
    "exact cells.\n",
    "\n",
    "To check whether composing just the 6 corner policies this way is actually *correct*,\n",
    "not merely plausible, we build one more exact ground truth: `product_policy_iteration`,\n",
    "full policy iteration over the real product space (grid state x automaton state, ~327\n",
    "pairs here) with a sparse +1 reward on task completion -- no basis restriction, no FSA\n",
    "value-iteration shortcut, just the true optimum for the whole non-Markovian task.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Result, verified by direct run:** `meta_fsa_value_iteration` converges in 3 sweeps\n",
    "over the 4-state automaton to\n",
    "```\n",
    "W[u0] = [0.9044 0.8097 0.     0.     0.     0.    ]   (go get coffee -- C1 or C2)\n",
    "W[u1] = [0.     0.     0.     0.     0.9135 0.9321]   (then mail -- M1 or M2)\n",
    "W[u2] = [0.     0.     1.     1.     0.     0.    ]   (then office -- O1 or O2)\n",
    "W[u3] = [0.     0.     0.     0.     0.     0.    ]   (done)\n",
    "```\n",
    "and the exact product-MDP ground truth confirms the composed plan is optimal *at the\n",
    "state that matters*: `V*(start, u0) = V^composed(start, u0) = 0.8097`, exactly, with\n",
    "zero additional training beyond the 6 single-objective corner policies already trained\n",
    "above. It is not exact everywhere in the product space (33 of 327 (state,\n",
    "automaton-state) pairs differ from the true optimum -- unsurprising, since `Pi_corners`\n",
    "is TD-learned, not exact, and untouched by Section 9's DST-style exact-basis argument),\n",
    "but the non-Markovian \"coffee, then mail, then office\" task is solved correctly from\n",
    "the state that was actually queried, purely by recombining an existing policy basis."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 26,
   "id": "044eb2a172b2",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Automaton-state weight vectors (SFFSAValueIteration.traverse, exact composition):\n",
      "  W[u0] = [0.9044 0.8097 0.     0.     0.     0.    ]\n",
      "  W[u1] = [0.     0.     0.     0.     0.9135 0.9321]\n",
      "  W[u2] = [0. 0. 1. 1. 0. 0.]\n",
      "  W[u3] = [0. 0. 0. 0. 0. 0.]\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from fsa.fsa import FiniteStateAutomaton\n",
    "\n",
    "symbols_to_phi = {sym: i for i, sym in enumerate(PHI_OBJ_TYPES)}\n",
    "fsa = FiniteStateAutomaton(symbols_to_phi)\n",
    "fsa.add_state(\"u0\")\n",
    "fsa.add_state(\"u1\")\n",
    "fsa.add_state(\"u2\")\n",
    "fsa.add_state(\"u3\")\n",
    "fsa.add_transition(\"u0\", \"u1\", [\"C1\", \"C2\"])  # get coffee\n",
    "fsa.add_transition(\"u1\", \"u2\", [\"M1\", \"M2\"])  # then mail\n",
    "fsa.add_transition(\"u2\", \"u3\", [\"O1\", \"O2\"])  # then office (u3 terminal -- task done)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def own_greedy_actions_any(sf_table, w):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Like own_greedy_actions, but over ALL office_states -- including object cells,\n",
    "    which meta_policy_iteration treats as absorbing sources and this must not.\"\"\"\n",
    "    return {s: int(np.argmax(sf_table[s] @ w)) for s in office_states}\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def meta_policy_iteration_from_any(w, Pi_base, W_base, gamma=GAMMA):\n",
    "    \"\"\"meta_policy_iteration, but solved for the value of FRESH-STARTING at any state\n",
    "    -- object cells included -- not just states that were already non-terminal sources\n",
    "    in the single-shot task. Object cells are still terminal as transition targets.\"\"\"\n",
    "    own_actions = [own_greedy_actions_any(sft, w_j) for sft, w_j in zip(Pi_base, W_base)]\n",
    "    meta_policy = {s: 0 for s in office_states}\n",
    "\n",
    "    while True:\n",
    "        A, b = np.eye(n_office_states), np.zeros(n_office_states)\n",
    "        for s in office_states:\n",
    "            i = office_state_idx[s]\n",
    "            ns, phi, term = office_step_deterministic(office_env, s, own_actions[meta_policy[s]][s])\n",
    "            b[i] = phi @ w\n",
    "            if not term:\n",
    "                A[i, office_state_idx[ns]] -= gamma\n",
    "        v = np.linalg.solve(A, b)\n",
    "        V = {s: v[office_state_idx[s]] for s in office_states}\n",
    "\n",
    "        stable = True\n",
    "        for s in office_states:\n",
    "            qs = []\n",
    "            for j in range(len(Pi_base)):\n",
    "                ns, phi, term = office_step_deterministic(office_env, s, own_actions[j][s])\n",
    "                qs.append(phi @ w + (0.0 if term else gamma * V[ns]))\n",
    "            best_j = int(np.argmax(qs))\n",
    "            stable &= best_j == meta_policy[s]\n",
    "            meta_policy[s] = best_j\n",
    "        if stable:\n",
    "            return meta_policy, V, own_actions\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def meta_fsa_value_iteration(fsa, Pi_base, W_base, exit_states_map, gamma=GAMMA, num_iters=100, tol=1e-10):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Direct port of SFFSAValueIteration.traverse (fsa/planning.py): backward value\n",
    "    iteration over the automaton graph, using an EXACT composed value in place of the\n",
    "    paper's trained gpi.max_q -- no product MDP, no retraining, just d-vector fixed-point\n",
    "    updates over |U| automaton states.\"\"\"\n",
    "    U = fsa.states\n",
    "    W = np.zeros((len(U), d))\n",
    "    for _ in range(num_iters):\n",
    "        W_old = W.copy()\n",
    "        for uidx, u in enumerate(U):\n",
    "            if fsa.is_terminal(u):\n",
    "                continue\n",
    "            total = np.zeros(d)\n",
    "            for vidx, v in enumerate(U):\n",
    "                if not fsa.graph.has_edge(u, v):\n",
    "                    continue\n",
    "                w_uv = np.zeros(d)\n",
    "                propositions = fsa.get_predicate((u, v))\n",
    "                idxs = [fsa.symbols_to_phi[p] for p in propositions]\n",
    "                if fsa.is_terminal(v):\n",
    "                    w_uv[idxs] = 1.0\n",
    "                else:\n",
    "                    for idx in idxs:\n",
    "                        e = exit_states_map[idx]\n",
    "                        _, V_e, _ = meta_policy_iteration_from_any(W[vidx], Pi_base, W_base, gamma)\n",
    "                        w_uv[idx] = V_e[e]\n",
    "                total += w_uv\n",
    "            W[uidx] = total\n",
    "        if np.allclose(W, W_old, atol=tol):\n",
    "            break\n",
    "    return {u: W[i] for i, u in enumerate(U)}\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "exit_states = office_env.core.exit_states\n",
    "W_fsa = meta_fsa_value_iteration(fsa, Pi_corners, simplex_corner_weights, exit_states)\n",
    "print(\"Automaton-state weight vectors (SFFSAValueIteration.traverse, exact composition):\")\n",
    "for u, w in W_fsa.items():\n",
    "    print(f\"  W[{u}] = {w.round(4)}\")"
   ]
  },
