   "source": [
    "## The math behind SF-FSA-VI\n",
    "\n",
    "**Setup.** MDP $(S, A, P, \\gamma)$, feature map $\\phi: S \\to \\mathbb{R}^d$ (one-hot on\n",
    "the object just touched, else $0$). For a policy $\\pi$, its successor feature is\n",
    "$$\\psi^\\pi(s,a) = \\mathbb{E}_\\pi\\Big[\\sum_{t\\ge 0} \\gamma^t \\phi(s_{t+1}) \\,\\Big|\\, s_0=s, a_0=a\\Big],$$\n",
    "so $\\psi^\\pi(s,a)\\cdot w$ is $\\pi$'s value under scalarization $w$. Given a basis\n",
    "$\\Pi=\\{\\pi_1,\\dots,\\pi_k\\}$ (trained at corner weights $w_1,\\dots,w_k$ -- `Pi_corners`\n",
    "above), GPI (Eq. 4) defines, for *any* weight $w$:\n",
    "$$V^\\Pi_{GPI}(s; w) = \\max_i \\max_a \\psi^{\\pi_i}(s,a)\\cdot w.$$\n",
    "Section 7's optimal-policy-transfer theorem: if $\\Pi$ spans the CCS,\n",
    "$V^\\Pi_{GPI}(\\cdot;w) = V^*_{single}(\\cdot;w)$ for *every* $w$, not just the corners\n",
    "solved for. That equality is the load-bearing fact everything below depends on.\n",
    "\n",
    "**The non-Markovian task as a reward machine.** $\\mathcal{U}=(U,u_0,F,\\delta)$:\n",
    "automaton states $U$, start $u_0$, terminal/accepting $F\\subseteq U$, transition\n",
    "$\\delta: U\\times\\Sigma \\to U$ over propositions $\\Sigma=\\{p_1,\\dots,p_d\\}$ (the 6\n",
    "objects). Proposition $p$ fires when the env enters its exit state $e_p$. The product\n",
    "MDP has states $(s,u)$, and -- because reward only ever fires at an exit state, and\n",
    "only changes $u$ there -- its Bellman optimality equation is\n",
    "$$V^*(s,u) = \\max_a \\sum_{s'} P(s'\\mid s,a)\\Big[r\\big((s,u),a,s'\\big) + \\gamma\\cdot\\mathbb{1}[u'\\notin F]\\cdot V^*(s',u')\\Big],$$\n",
    "with $u'=\\delta(u,\\ell(s,a,s'))$, $r=1$ exactly on the transition that completes the\n",
    "task. This is what `product_policy_iteration` solves directly, with no shortcuts.\n",
    "\n",
    "**The reduction that makes the small algorithm valid.** Define, for each live\n",
    "automaton state $u$, a vector $W(u)\\in\\mathbb{R}^d$:\n",
    "$$W(u)_p = \\begin{cases} 1 & \\delta(u,p)\\in F \\quad\\text{(satisfying $p$ finishes the task)}\\\\ V^*\\big(e_p,\\ \\delta(u,p)\\big) & \\delta(u,p)\\notin F \\quad\\text{(task continues under the next subtask)}\\\\ 0 & p \\text{ triggers no edge from } u\\end{cases}$$\n",
    "\n",
    "**Claim.** With this $W(u)$, the *ordinary single-task* value function under\n",
    "scalarization $W(u)$ equals the true product value:\n",
    "$V^*_{single}(s; W(u)) = V^*(s,u)$ for every $s$, not just at exit states. Why:\n",
    "touching any object $p$ while at automaton state $u$ contributes exactly\n",
    "$\\phi(s')\\cdot W(u) = W(u)_p$ to a single-task rollout -- and $W(u)_p$ was defined to\n",
    "be *precisely* \"1 if that finishes it, else the value of carrying on\" -- so scalarizing\n",
    "by $W(u)$ and solving the ordinary (Markovian, single-episode) problem is a faithful\n",
    "encoding of \"the task, given you're currently in automaton state $u$.\"\n",
    "\n",
    "Substituting $V^*(e_p,\\delta(u,p)) = V^*_{single}(e_p; W(\\delta(u,p)))$ (same equality,\n",
    "one level deeper) gives exactly the fixed-point system `meta_fsa_value_iteration`\n",
    "iterates:\n",
    "$$W(u)_p = 1 \\ \\ \\text{if } \\delta(u,p)\\in F, \\qquad W(u)_p = V^*_{single}\\big(e_p; W(\\delta(u,p))\\big) \\ \\ \\text{if } \\delta(u,p)\\notin F.$$\n",
    "For an **acyclic** automaton (our chain `u0 -> u1 -> u2 -> u3`), this is just backward\n",
    "induction over a DAG -- exact in at most $|U|$ sweeps (we saw 3, matching the chain\n",
    "length). For a cyclic reward machine, $\\gamma<1$ still makes the update a genuine\n",
    "contraction (each traversal costs $\\ge 1$ environment step, so $\\ge 1$ factor of\n",
    "$\\gamma$), so value iteration still converges, just asymptotically rather than in\n",
    "finitely many exact sweeps.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Where GPI enters, and why Office isn't exact but DST would be.**\n",
    "`meta_fsa_value_iteration` needs $V^*_{single}(e_p;\\cdot)$ -- and that's exactly\n",
    "$V^\\Pi_{GPI}$ (or, as implemented here, the more restrictive exact composed value from\n",
    "`meta_policy_iteration_from_any`). The whole correctness argument above collapses to:\n",
    "**`meta_fsa_value_iteration` computes the true $V^*(s,u)$ if and only if\n",
    "$V^\\Pi_{GPI} = V^*_{single}$ for every weight $W(u)$ the recursion visits.** That's\n",
    "precisely the condition Section 9 (in the DST notebook) proved *exactly* for DST's\n",
    "2-policy reduced basis (zero mismatch, everywhere, provably) -- so running this same\n",
    "FSA construction on DST with that basis would give a *provably exact* non-Markovian\n",
    "plan. Office's `Pi_corners` is TD-learned, not exact, so $V^\\Pi_{GPI}\\ne V^*_{single}$\n",
    "in general (only close) -- which is exactly the 33/327 product-state mismatch measured\n",
    "above, not a flaw in the FSA machinery itself."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6ea45805a6a6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Algorithm: `MetaFSAValueIteration`$(\\mathcal{U}, \\Pi, \\{w_i\\}, \\{e_p\\}, \\gamma)$**\n",
    "\n",
    "*Input:* reward machine $\\mathcal{U}=(U,u_0,F,\\delta)$ over propositions $\\Sigma$;\n",
    "policy basis $\\Pi=\\{\\pi_1,\\dots,\\pi_k\\}$ with SFs $\\psi_{\\pi_i}$ and their own training\n",
    "weights $w_i$; exit-state map $p \\mapsto e_p$; discount $\\gamma$.\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Initialize $W(u) \\leftarrow 0 \\in \\mathbb{R}^d$ for every live automaton state\n",
    "   $u \\in U\\setminus F$.\n",
    "2. **Repeat** until $W$ stops changing (for an acyclic $\\mathcal{U}$ this takes at most\n",
    "   $|U|$ sweeps -- exact backward induction over the automaton DAG, not an asymptotic\n",
    "   limit):\n",
    "   For every $u \\in U\\setminus F$:\n",
    "   $$W(u) \\ \\leftarrow\\ \\sum_{v\\,:\\,(u,v)\\in\\delta} \\ \\sum_{p\\,\\in\\,\\text{label}(u,v)} \\mathbf{e}_p \\cdot \\begin{cases} 1 & v \\in F \\\\ V^\\Pi\\big(e_p;\\ W(v)\\big) & v \\notin F \\end{cases}$$\n",
    "   where $\\mathbf{e}_p$ is the $p$-th standard basis vector of $\\mathbb{R}^d$ (write\n",
    "   the result into just that coordinate), and\n",
    "   $V^\\Pi(e;w) = \\max_i \\max_a \\psi_{\\pi_i}(e,a)\\cdot w$ is the GPI value of the basis\n",
    "   (`meta_policy_iteration_from_any`'s exact composed value, in the code above -- see\n",
    "   the previous cell for why *which* $V^\\Pi$ you plug in determines whether this whole\n",
    "   algorithm is exact or only approximately correct).\n",
    "3. **Return** $W: U\\setminus F \\to \\mathbb{R}^d$.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Acting**, once $W$ has converged: at product-state $(s,u)$, take\n",
    "$a = \\arg\\max_a \\max_i \\psi_{\\pi_i}(s,a)\\cdot W(u)$ (ordinary GPI, using $u$'s own\n",
    "weight vector); observe the result; if it is an exit state $e_p$ with\n",
    "$\\delta(u,p)$ defined, update $u \\leftarrow \\delta(u,p)$, otherwise $u$ is unchanged.\n",
    "No new policy is ever trained -- $u$ only ever selects *which* of the $k$ already-known\n",
    "weight vectors $W(u)$ to hand to the same fixed basis $\\Pi$.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why this is cheap.** Each sweep costs $O(|U| \\cdot \\bar{d}_{\\text{out}})$ queries to\n",
    "$V^\\Pi$, where $\\bar d_{\\text{out}}$ is the automaton's out-degree -- $|U|=4$ states,\n",
    "at most 2 propositions per edge here, versus solving `product_policy_iteration`'s full\n",
    "$|S|\\times|U|$ product MDP (327 states) directly. The saving compounds with task size:\n",
    "$|U|$ grows only with the *task's* complexity (how many subgoals, in what order), while\n",
    "$|S|\\times|U|$ grows with the *environment* too -- the whole point of reusing a fixed\n",
    "policy basis instead of re-planning over the product space from scratch."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "06e77387a939",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Timing: solving fresh vs. composing the basis, for a single fixed weight\n",
    "\n",
    "The \"why this is cheap\" note above claims a saving that scales with the *task* --\n",
    "`meta_fsa_value_iteration` costs `O(|U|)` composed-value queries instead of solving a\n",
    "full `|S| x |U|` product MDP. That's a different claim from \"composing is faster than\n",
    "solving a single fixed-weight task from scratch,\" and it's worth checking that second\n",
    "claim directly rather than assuming it: `office_policy_iteration(w)` (fresh exact\n",
    "policy iteration, 4 primitive actions, no reuse) vs. `meta_policy_iteration(w,\n",
    "Pi_corners, W_base)` (exact composition over the already-trained 6-policy basis, but 6\n",
    "meta-actions instead of 4) -- both are exact linear-algebra solves given the same known\n",
    "deterministic model, so there's no a priori reason composing has to win."
   ]
  },
