   "source": [
    "def compare_to_optimal(V_candidate, V_opt, tol=1e-6):\n",
    "    mismatched = [s for s in nonterminal if not np.isclose(V_candidate[s], V_opt[s], atol=tol)]\n",
    "    return len(mismatched), mismatched\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"{len(nonterminal)} non-terminal states, {len(bench_weights)} test weights\\n\")\n",
    "header = (\"w\", \"sum V*\", \"sum V_naive\", \"mismatch_naive\", \"sum V_gpi\", \"mismatch_gpi\")\n",
    "print(f\"{header[0]:40s} {header[1]:>10s} {header[2]:>12s} {header[3]:>15s} {header[4]:>10s} {header[5]:>13s}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "all_exact = True\n",
    "for w in bench_weights:\n",
    "    _, V_opt, _ = office_policy_iteration_timed(w)\n",
    "    _, V_naive, _ = meta_policy_iteration_gpi_init(w, Pi_corners, simplex_corner_weights, gpi_init=False)\n",
    "    _, V_gpi, _ = meta_policy_iteration_gpi_init(w, Pi_corners, simplex_corner_weights, gpi_init=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "    n_mis_naive, _ = compare_to_optimal(V_naive, V_opt)\n",
    "    n_mis_gpi, _ = compare_to_optimal(V_gpi, V_opt)\n",
    "    all_exact &= (n_mis_naive == 0) and (n_mis_gpi == 0)\n",
    "\n",
    "    sum_opt = sum(V_opt[s] for s in nonterminal)\n",
    "    sum_naive = sum(V_naive[s] for s in nonterminal)\n",
    "    sum_gpi = sum(V_gpi[s] for s in nonterminal)\n",
    "\n",
    "    print(f\"{str(w.round(2)):40s} {sum_opt:10.4f} {sum_naive:12.4f} {n_mis_naive:8d}/{len(nonterminal)} \"\n",
    "          f\"{sum_gpi:10.4f} {n_mis_gpi:6d}/{len(nonterminal)}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\nall three (scratch, naive-init meta, gpi-init meta) reach the identical exact \"\n",
    "      f\"optimum for all {len(bench_weights)} weights: {all_exact}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d75c13a0e70d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Reading the numbers.** Composing is *not* reliably faster than solving fresh here --\n",
    "speedup ranges 0.53x-2.18x across weights with no consistent winner, and the mean is\n",
    "actually slightly *below* 1x. That makes sense once you look at the sweep counts:\n",
    "`meta_policy_iteration` evaluates 6 meta-actions per state per sweep against\n",
    "`office_policy_iteration`'s 4 primitive actions, which roughly cancels out any benefit\n",
    "from starting from \"smarter\" candidates. **Both are already-exact, model-based linear\n",
    "algebra** -- there's no learning happening in either one, so there's no learning-time\n",
    "gap to close.\n",
    "\n",
    "The real saving shows up one level up: training a *new* corner policy from raw\n",
    "environment interaction (Q-learning, `NUM_STEPS_PER_POLICY=100_000` steps) takes\n",
    "~25x longer than composing the *existing* basis exactly for a brand-new weight, and\n",
    "that gap would only widen for a harder environment (more steps to converge) or a\n",
    "more expensive real-world rollout (no free `office_step_deterministic` oracle to query\n",
    "instead of interacting with the real system). That's the actual claim this whole\n",
    "notebook has been building toward: not \"planning is faster than planning,\" but\n",
    "\"reusing a small trained basis is faster than training a new policy from scratch\" --\n",
    "and, per the FSA section above, \"planning over the automaton is cheaper than planning\n",
    "over the full product MDP,\" a separate saving that compounds with this one."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "adaptivefsaplan",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Planning: an adaptive, certified basis for `meta_fsa_value_iteration`\n",
    "\n",
    "**What's being replaced.** `meta_fsa_value_iteration` above calls\n",
    "`meta_policy_iteration_from_any(W[vidx], Pi_base, W_base, gamma)` at every automaton\n",
    "edge, every sweep, always against the SAME fixed, pre-trained `Pi_corners` -- all 6\n",
    "corner policies, trained once via TD-learning (`train_ok`'s `new_policy`/Q-learning\n",
    "recipe), independent of which FSA later uses them. Two separate problems with that,\n",
    "worth fixing separately:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Correctness.** `Pi_corners` is TD-learned, not exact -- `own_greedy_actions_any`\n",
    "   picks each policy's OWN action from a noisy Q-table, so even though\n",
    "   `meta_policy_iteration_from_any`'s composition step is exact linear algebra *given*\n",
    "   that action menu, the menu itself can be wrong. That's the source of the 33/327\n",
    "   product-state mismatches already measured above, not the composition mechanism.\n",
    "2. **Basis size assumed, not verified.** All 6 corners get trained upfront regardless\n",
    "   of which FSA will use them. The section above (\"Is the exact meta-policy exact?\")\n",
    "   already established that Office's *global* structure needs all `k=6` for composition\n",
    "   to be exact at an *arbitrary* weight -- unlike DST, there is no smaller basis that\n",
    "   works everywhere. So this is *not* expected to shrink below 6 for THIS specific\n",
    "   3-edge \"coffee -> mail -> office\" FSA, which touches all 6 objects across its edges.\n",
    "   The place it should matter is a *different* FSA that only touches a subset of\n",
    "   objects (e.g. \"just get coffee\") -- there, on-demand training should stop at 2\n",
    "   corners instead of paying for 6 upfront. Worth being honest about this going in,\n",
    "   not discovering it after the fact.\n",
    "\n",
    "**The plan, concretely:**\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Build exact corner policies.** Nothing in this notebook currently builds a full,\n",
    "   exact SF *table* (`Psi(s,a)` for every action, not just a scalar `V`) the way DST's\n",
    "   `solve_task_exact` does -- `office_policy_iteration` only returns `(policy, V)`.\n",
    "   Write `office_solve_task_exact(w)`: run `office_policy_iteration(w)` for the optimal\n",
    "   policy, then fill in `Psi(s,a)` for every action exactly as DST's `solve_task_exact`\n",
    "   does (`phi(s,a)` if `a` is terminal, else `phi(s,a) + gamma * V[next]`). This removes\n",
    "   problem (1) outright, independent of basis size: whatever gets composed is provably\n",
    "   exact given the menu, and the menu itself is now exact too.\n",
    "\n",
    "2. **Write the Office Bellman certificate.** Direct port of `bellman_gap` from the DST\n",
    "   notebook's Section 13/15: one full backup over the REAL 4-action space (not the\n",
    "   restricted meta-action menu) against a candidate `V`, using `office_step_deterministic`\n",
    "   for the oracle. Zero gap everywhere -> the composed value is exact, no ground truth\n",
    "   needed to know it (`product_policy_iteration` stays available as an independent\n",
    "   check, same role Section 11's dense sweep played for DST, not as part of the\n",
    "   certificate itself).\n",
    "\n",
    "3. **Adaptive composition inside the automaton sweep.** New function,\n",
    "   `meta_policy_iteration_certified(w, Pi_base, W_base)`: try composing from the\n",
    "   CURRENT shared base first; run the certificate; if it fails, solve exactly at `w`\n",
    "   via `office_solve_task_exact`, add the result to the shared base, and use that. This\n",
    "   is called in place of `meta_policy_iteration_from_any` inside a new\n",
    "   `meta_fsa_value_iteration_adaptive`, which starts with an EMPTY (or minimal) base --\n",
    "   not the pre-trained 6 -- and grows it purely from what the automaton sweep actually\n",
    "   queries. Since `traverse`'s `W[vidx]` vectors are sparse (each edge's weight only has\n",
    "   support on the 1-2 objects that edge's propositions name -- e.g. `W[u0]` only ever\n",
    "   touches the C1/C2 coordinates), each individual certified-composition call should\n",
    "   only ever need the corners relevant to *that* edge, not all 6 -- worth confirming by\n",
    "   logging which corners actually get added and in what order, not assumed.\n",
    "\n",
    "4. **Verify and benchmark.** Check the resulting `W_fsa_adaptive` against\n",
    "   `product_policy_iteration`'s ground truth exactly as the existing section does\n",
    "   (expect 0/327 mismatches now, not 33, since every composed value is either\n",
    "   certified-exact or was a fallback exact solve). Report: final basis size (is it\n",
    "   really 6 for this particular 3-object-pair FSA, confirming point 2 above, or does it\n",
    "   land lower even here?), how many certified-composition calls succeeded vs. how many\n",
    "   triggered a fallback solve, and wall-clock against training all 6 corners via\n",
    "   TD-learning upfront (the existing `~25x` composing-vs-training-from-scratch number\n",
    "   already measured above is the relevant baseline for whatever fallback solves DO\n",
    "   happen -- worth reusing that framing rather than re-deriving it).\n",
    "\n",
    "**One open design question, not yet resolved**: when a fallback solve is needed, should\n",
    "it solve exactly at the *literal* `W[vidx]` vector encountered mid-sweep (e.g.\n",
    "`[0.9044, 0.8097, 0, 0, 0, 0]`), or at the one-hot corner weight matching whichever\n",
    "object dominates that vector? Office's own structure (every episode ends on first\n",
    "object touched, so the true optimal policy for *any* weight is always \"go straight to\n",
    "the single best object\") suggests solving at the one-hot corner might already be\n",
    "sufficient for any weight sharing that same argmax object -- but that should be\n",
    "verified directly, not assumed, before relying on it to avoid one-off exact solves at\n",
    "every distinct `W[vidx]` the sweep happens to produce."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "adaptivefsaimplmd",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Implementation\n",
    "\n",
    "Three pieces, matching the plan above: exact building blocks, the adaptive FSA-VI loop\n",
    "itself, then verification reusing `product_policy_iteration`'s ground truth already\n",
    "computed above -- no need to resolve it."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 32,
   "id": "adaptivefsaimplcode1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "n_actions = office_env.action_space.n\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def office_policy_iteration_from_any(w, gamma=GAMMA):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Like office_policy_iteration, but object cells are valid non-absorbing SOURCE\n",
    "    states too (still terminal as destinations) -- ground truth for exit-state values,\n",
    "    the unrestricted-action counterpart to meta_policy_iteration_from_any.\"\"\"\n",
    "    policy = {s: 0 for s in office_states}\n",
    "    while True:\n",
    "        A, b = np.eye(n_office_states), np.zeros(n_office_states)\n",
    "        for s in office_states:\n",
    "            i = office_state_idx[s]\n",
    "            ns, phi, term = office_step_deterministic(office_env, s, policy[s])\n",
    "            b[i] = phi @ w\n",
    "            if not term:\n",
    "                A[i, office_state_idx[ns]] -= gamma\n",
    "        v = np.linalg.solve(A, b)\n",
    "        V = {s: v[office_state_idx[s]] for s in office_states}\n",
    "        stable = True\n",
    "        for s in office_states:\n",
    "            qs = []\n",
    "            for a in range(n_actions):\n",
    "                ns, phi, term = office_step_deterministic(office_env, s, a)\n",
    "                qs.append(phi @ w + (0.0 if term else gamma * V[ns]))\n",
    "            best_a = int(np.argmax(qs))\n",
    "            stable &= best_a == policy[s]\n",
    "            policy[s] = best_a\n",
    "        if stable:\n",
    "            return policy, V\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def office_solve_task_exact(w, gamma=GAMMA):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Exact SF table Psi(s,a) for EVERY action and EVERY state (object cells included\n",
    "    as sources) -- Office's counterpart to DST's solve_task_exact. The scalar V from\n",
    "    office_policy_iteration_from_any is only for PICKING the policy -- the SF table\n",
    "    needs a SEPARATE, vector-valued evaluation of that fixed policy (same two-step\n",
    "    pattern DST's solve_task_exact uses); reusing the scalar V directly here would\n",
    "    silently broadcast it across all feature dimensions instead of accumulating the\n",
    "    real per-feature vector.\"\"\"\n",
    "    policy, _ = office_policy_iteration_from_any(w, gamma)\n",
    "    A, b = np.eye(n_office_states), np.zeros((n_office_states, d))\n",
    "    for s in office_states:\n",
    "        i = office_state_idx[s]\n",
    "        ns, phi, term = office_step_deterministic(office_env, s, policy[s])\n",
    "        b[i] = phi\n",
    "        if not term:\n",
    "            A[i, office_state_idx[ns]] -= gamma\n",
    "    V_vec = np.linalg.solve(A, b)\n",
    "    V_vec = {s: V_vec[office_state_idx[s]] for s in office_states}\n",
    "\n",
    "    psi = {}\n",
    "    for s in office_states:\n",
    "        table = np.zeros((n_actions, d))\n",
    "        for a in range(n_actions):\n",
    "            ns, phi, term = office_step_deterministic(office_env, s, a)\n",
    "            table[a] = phi if term else phi + gamma * V_vec[ns]\n",
    "        psi[s] = table\n",
    "    return psi\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def office_bellman_gap_from_any(w, V, gamma=GAMMA):\n",
    "    \"\"\"One full Bellman backup over the REAL 4-action space against a candidate V,\n",
    "    object cells included as sources -- no ground truth needed to trust a zero gap.\"\"\"\n",
    "    gaps = {}\n",
    "    for s in office_states:\n",
    "        qs = []\n",
    "        for a in range(n_actions):\n",
    "            ns, phi, term = office_step_deterministic(office_env, s, a)\n",
    "            qs.append(phi @ w + (0.0 if term else gamma * V[ns]))\n",
    "        gaps[s] = max(qs) - V[s]\n",
    "    return gaps\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def meta_policy_iteration_certified(w, Pi_base, W_base, gamma=GAMMA, cert_tol=1e-6):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Compose from the CURRENT base; certify; fall back to an exact solve + grow the\n",
    "    base if the certificate fails. Returns the (possibly grown) base too, so it threads\n",
    "    through the FSA sweep below.\"\"\"\n",
    "    if Pi_base:\n",
    "        meta_policy, V, own_actions = meta_policy_iteration_from_any(w, Pi_base, W_base, gamma)\n",
    "        worst_gap = max(office_bellman_gap_from_any(w, V, gamma).values())\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        worst_gap = np.inf\n",
    "    if worst_gap > cert_tol:\n",
    "        psi_new = office_solve_task_exact(w, gamma)\n",
    "        Pi_base = Pi_base + [psi_new]\n",
    "        W_base = W_base + [w]\n",
    "        meta_policy, V, own_actions = meta_policy_iteration_from_any(w, Pi_base, W_base, gamma)\n",
    "        fell_back = True\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        fell_back = False\n",
    "    return meta_policy, V, own_actions, Pi_base, W_base, fell_back"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
